[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged on subject lines ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)),
so every report about a wrong date went into it. Read by tenant, booking form and what people
describe, it holds three problems. One fix will not close them all, so each has its own ticket:

| problem | what breaks | ticket |
|---|---|---|
| `parser` | day-first dates are read month first | [#1](https://github.com/pablocherryfender/mega-dot-dev/issues/1) |
| `hint` | the booking-v3 form tells people to type the month first | [#2](https://github.com/pablocherryfender/mega-dot-dev/issues/2) |
| one-day move | a date moves by one day, with no month/day swap | [#3](https://github.com/pablocherryfender/mega-dot-dev/issues/3) |

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is not one known issue. Fixing the parser leaves the other two open.
</Callout>

## What the desk's view shows

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table counts each report once, by id, and places it by tenant and booking form, not by the
intake tag. `hint` is its own problem now, with its own ticket. The reports in the note under
`parser` are the one-day moves: they are filed under `parser` by tenant, but a month/day swap
does not explain them, so they are tracked apart. The `parser` ticket counts its row without them.

## The problems

### `parser`: day-first dates read month first

The shared parser reads every date month first. Every tenant on file writes the day first, so a
booking for the seventh of April goes out for the fourth of July. This is the bug #4471 describes,
and it hits every tenant through the app, email and the booking-v2 form.

Fix: parse dates in the tenant's locale (`dayFirst()` in `causes.ts` already asks the platform).

### `hint`: booking-v3 tells people to type month first

The booking-v3 form prints a month-first hint under its date field, then reads the date the
tenant's way, day first. People type what the hint says, and the date comes out flipped. Only
tenants on booking-v3 have it, and only through the form, so the parser fix does not touch it.

Fix: print the tenant's own order under the field, as booking-v2 does.

### One-day move: dates move by one day, no swap

These reports describe a date that moved by one day: an invite that says Tuesday while the
calendar says Monday, every booking in one month one day off, a client in Lisbon who got Tuesday
while a client in Toronto got Monday, an invite that arrived before the booking was made. The desk
had already listed them in `desk-notes.json`.

Likely cause, not yet confirmed: a date converted through UTC or the viewer's time zone, so it
lands on the day before. Engineering should check how invite dates are stored and rendered.

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Lessons

- A subject line tells you what people noticed, not what broke. Merge on cause, not subject.
- Read the footnotes under a count: they can hold a problem of their own.

